  "coverageShareIntro": "Help show where the mesh reaches. While a wardrive runs, what your radio hears is added to the public NOTORYX coverage map. Nothing is shared until you agree.",
  "coverageShareStart": "Start sharing",
  "coverageConsentTitle": "Share coverage?",
  "coverageConsentBody": "While a wardrive is running, the app notes what your radio hears in each hexagon (about 0.9 km across) in 15-minute blocks, and keeps it on this phone for 7 days.\n\nSent to coverage.meshmayhem.org for each hexagon: the hexagon, the 15-minute time, how many packets were heard, the best SNR and RSSI, and the short IDs of repeaters heard directly with their SNR. With Live or Delayed, also: a coverage key made on this phone (not your radio's identity) that signs every upload so you can erase it later, your mapper name if you set one, and repeaters you know that advertised a position (key, name, position, advert time).\n\nNever sent: your GPS track or exact position, messages, contacts or your radio's identity. The first and last hexagons of each drive stay on the phone unless you turn that off.\n\nAnonymous sends no key, name or repeater list, rounds times to the day and waits a day. It can't be erased later.\n\nYou can stop sharing or erase your uploads at any time.",
